The UE RF requirements for FR1 and FR2 for the support of Carrier Aggregation in Terrestrial Networks are specified in the sub-clauses listed hereafter. Note: differences between the FR1 and FR2 specifications (e.g. sub-clause appearing only in one specification, title - slightly - different) are highlighted in blue below. 1) For FR1 in TS 38.101-1 [3]: General (Clause 5) 5.2A Operating bands for CA 5.3A UE channel bandwidth for CA 5.4A Channel arrangement for CA 5.5A Configurations for CA Transmitter characteristics (Clause 6) 6.1A General 6.2A Transmitter power for CA 6.3A Output power dynamics for CA 6.4A Transmit signal quality for CA 6.5A Output RF spectrum emissions for CA Receiver characteristics (Clause 7) 7.1A General 7.3A Reference sensitivity for CA 7.4A Maximum input level for CA 7.5A Adjacent channel selectivity for CA 7.6A Blocking characteristics for CA 7.7A Spurious response for CA 7.8A Intermodulation characteristics for CA 7.9A Spurious emissions for CA 7.10A Power imbalance for CA 2) For FR2 in TS 38.101-2 [4]: General (Clause 5) 5.2A Operating bands for CA 5.3A UE channel bandwidth for CA 5.4A Channel arrangement for CA 5.5A Configurations for CA Transmitter characteristics (Clause 6) 6.2A Transmitter power for CA 6.3A Output power dynamics for CA 6.4A Transmit signal quality for CA 6.5A Output RF spectrum emissions for CA 6.6A Beam correspondence for CA Receiver characteristics (Clause 7) 7.3A Reference sensitivity for DL CA 7.4A Maximum input level for DL CA 7.5A Adjacent channel selectivity for DL CA 7.6A Blocking characteristics for DL CA It can be observed that: For CA-related sections present in both FR1 and FR2 specifications, the same sub-clause numbering has been used in FR1 and FR2 specifications. Sections that are not present in either FR1 or FR2 specification have just been omitted in the related specification. Observation 2: A very similar structure has been used to specify CA UE RF requirements in FR1 and FR2 TN specifications.

